+
+
+if __name__ == "__main__":
+    print(json.dumps(selftest(), indent=2, sort_keys=True))

codex
The first full gate run found two useful facts: the shipping attacks all failed and the BFS reference solved 8/8 as Track B requires, but the tiny demo’s port-switched \(K_{2,2}\) blocks split into multiple components, giving four valid anchored cuts. That does not affect shipping, but it weakens the worked example and exact density claim. I’m replacing only the demo’s auxiliary graph by one connected even cycle; the shipping construction remains the regular block-trap graph.
apply patch
