codex
The successful replies reveal the real flaw: models are not using the planted tag hint at all—they mechanically two-colour the auxiliary graph. So increasing tag width is the wrong axis, and the 300-operation cap blocks increasing \(n\) enough. I’m preserving this budget-bound transcript, then replacing the easy bipartite auxiliary graph with an exact 3-XOR-to-MAXCUT gadget composition: the cut optimum remains known term-by-term, but the standard certificate algorithm becomes Gaussian elimination rather than BFS. This stays inside the paper’s native cut-admissibility objects and the same Section 3 identity.
